{"created": "2024-10-02T12:33:55.773565+00:00", "modified": "2025-11-04T12:52:49.723365+00:00", "id": 13869065, "conceptrecid": "13869064", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.13869064", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "metadata": {"title": "Urban Vegetation Data - Canopy Height Model (Brussels Capital Region, 2021)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "publication_date": "2024-10-01", "description": "<p>This GIS dataset was created for the following scientific publication, as part of the EU-funded&nbsp;<a href=\"https://coolschools.eu/\">Cool Schools</a>&nbsp;research project (under Grant Agreement No. 101003758) : Gallez, E., Canters, F., Gadeyne, S., &amp; Bar&oacute;, F. (2024).&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2212041624000846?via%3Dihub\">A multi-indicator distributive justice approach to assess school-related green infrastructure benefits in Brussels - ScienceDirect</a>. Ecosystem Services, 70, 101677. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoser.2024.101677.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><em>Very-High Resolution Canopy Height Model (resolution : 25cm), distinguishing between 4 vegetation types (trees, high shrubs, low shrubs and grass) in the Brussels Capital Region.</em></p>\n<p><em>Coordinate system : Lambert_Belge_72.</em></p>\n<p><em>The CHM was built on </em><em>:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>VHR aerial orthophotos (visible RGB and NIR) (&ldquo;UrbIS-Ortho N-S, 2021&rdquo;) for the Brussels Capital Region, of 5x5cm resolution&nbsp; Source: Paradigm. (2021). UrbIS-Ortho N-S. Paradigm.Brussels. <a href=\"https://datastore.brussels/web/data/dataset/fec72767-d6b6-41b9-a767-616df2779aae#access\">https://datastore.brussels/web/urbisdownload</a>. &nbsp;and;</em></li>\n<li><em>digital terrain models (DSM and DTM) of 50x50cm, captured on 22/09/2021. Paradigm.Brussels. </em><em>Source: Paradigm. (2021). DSM / DTM. Paradigm.Brussels. <a href=\"https://datastore.brussels/web/data/dataset/1d7bd49d-fe83-4388-af85-6f5dc8ec7909#access\">https://datastore.brussels/web/urbisdownload.</a></em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Both the orthophotos and digital terrain models were resampled to a 25x25cm resolution, using a bilinear interpolation method. </em></p>\n<p><em>The Canopy Height Model was then created by selecting NDVI values of 0.2 and higher, - a commonly used threshold value to distinguish vegetated land from built land (Hashim et al., 2019) -, </em><em>and vegetation height thresholds of &lt; 0.5m (for grass), 0.5 - 2m (for low shrubs), 2 - 5m (for high shrubs), and &gt; 5m (for trees) (Derkzen et al., 2015; Sankey et al., 2018). </em><em>Green roofs were excluded.The CHM raster was then converted to polygon features.&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p><em>Classification :</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>From 0 to 0.5 m (nDSM value) : gridcode 1 = </em><em>grass</em></li>\n<li><em>From 0.5 to 2 m (nDSM value): gridcode 2 =&nbsp;</em><em>low shrubs</em></li>\n<li><em>From 2 to 5 m (nDSM value): gridcode 3 =</em><em> high shrubs</em></li>\n<li><em>From 5 to 113.96 m (nDSM value): gridcode 4 = </em><em>trees</em></li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Gallez, Elsa", "affiliation": "Vrije Universiteit Brussel", "orcid": "0000-0002-2198-2504"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Bar\u00f3, Francesc", "affiliation": "Vrije Universiteit Brussel", "type": "ProjectLeader", "orcid": "0000-0002-0145-6320"}], "dates": [{"type": "created"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "101003758", "internal_id": "04af9zr29::101003758", "funder": {"name": "Innoviris"}, "title": "COOLSCHOOLS - Realizing potentials of nature-based climate shelters in school environments for urban transformation", "url": "https://coolschools.eu/"}], "communities": [{"id": "coolschools"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "13869064"}}]}}, "title": "Urban Vegetation Data - Canopy Height Model (Brussels Capital Region, 2021)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13869065", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13869065?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.13869065", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869064", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13869064", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13869064", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.13869064", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:13869065/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:13869065/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/13869065/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/13869065/quota-increase", "requests": "htt